; Rescued, not a starter: the Court's second chapter wizard, freed by tracing the door he sketched in charcoal on the
; Gallery's end wall, dot to dot (.ai/chapter-wizards.md 4.8). The boy of the Chinese tale whose brush made real
; whatever he painted, kept here to paint the dark wizard's portraits. His passive is Paint What Is Needed, the one
; axis no other wizard owns: once a run, below a quarter of his health, a flask is painted at his feet. He opens on
; Ink Ring (Water + Darkness) since 2026-11-10 (Eric: "would it make sense for ink ring to be his starting spell
; instead?" - "Yes, add it"; .ai/character-fit.md row 21): his brush, walked - a line that becomes real is his legend.
; His final form, The Painted Door, moved onto it from the crow Familiar he opened on before (as the crow every run from
; 2026-11-09; dog, crow or cat before that). Everyone else earns Ink Ring only as him (the Cormorant feat, in-flight
; 84). Whenever he takes the Familiar, his crow is still painted in ink (Familiar.PaintsInInk).
